            <div xml:id="d659">

                <pb facs="0688" n="590" sameAs="frus:frus1930v02/pg590"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51/5261</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-04-15">April 15, 1930</date>.<lb/>[Received May
                        22.]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 147</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to the Department’s telegram
                    No. 124, of April 8, 4 p.m., authorizing me to address a note to the Minister
                    for Foreign Affairs urging that some practical measure be taken without further
                    delay for the relief of American creditors, I have the honor <pb facs="0689"
                        n="591" xml:id="pg591"/> to enclose a copy of my note No. 57, of April 12,
                    1930, to Dr. Wang in the matter.</p>
                <p>Let me add, with reference to paragraph two of my telegram No. 247, of April 3, 9
                    p.m., that I have sent my British Colleague a copy of this note.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Nelson Trusler
                    Johnson</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d659-a1.xml" xpointer="d659-a1"/>
            </div>
